wash (0.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * agent: wash runs coding agents itself, over the Agent Client Protocol.
    A new Agent app (com.wash.ai) opens a session in a chosen folder with a
    chosen agent, streams the conversation, and renders markdown, tables and
    inline images. The empty window is the launcher; one window per session.
  * agent: permission requests arrive as structured data rather than being
    inferred from terminal output, and land in the same approval queue the
    sidebar already rendered. Answer from the transcript or the sidebar —
    both are views of one queue — with keyboard shortcuts on the buttons.
  * agent: the agent's OWN settings are on the window: approval mode (for
    Codex, read-only / agent / full-access), model, reasoning effort and
    plan mode, all through session/set_config_option. wash asks the agent to
    change its policy rather than routing around it, so an organisation's
    pinned mode still holds.
  * agent: Stop a running turn, see the context it has burned, and pick from
    the agent's own slash commands as you type one.
  * agent: sessions are named by what they are about, using the title the
    agent writes itself — shown as the window title, in the sidebar and in
    the History menu. Closing a window asks whether to detach (it keeps
    working, reattach from the sidebar) or terminate (it joins the history).
  * agent: File / Edit / Session / History menus, including saving the
    transcript and copying the last reply.
  * agent: REMOVED the previous mechanism — hook installation into a
    vendor's settings file, the OSC 7770 status channel, the per-tab
    decision socket and the typed-`y` output tap, along with the
    wash-agent-hook helper and `wash agent-hooks`. A settings file an older
    wash wrote still names that binary; delete the wash entries by hand.
  * ui: shared <MenuBar> in @wash/ui, extracted from wash-edit now that a
    second app wants one.
  * term: restored the wash environment for terminals (TERM, $WASH_BIN_DIR
    on PATH, display hints), lost when the agent decision socket was removed.

 -- sirmick <sirmick@gmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 06:44:26 -0700

wash (0.11.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * term: agent-aware terminals. A coding agent (Claude Code and friends)
    running in a wash terminal is now visible to the desktop: a state dot on
    the tab chip and a clause in the status line (blue working / amber needs
    input / green done), driven by an OSC 7770 status channel parsed in the
    pty layer plus a foreground-process check that needs no install.
  * term: transition notifications. A toast when an agent wants your input
    or finishes a turn, rate-limited per tab, with click-to-focus landing on
    the terminal that raised it, and an amber attention dot on its taskbar
    pill until you visit it.
  * term: agent approval policy. Each pty gets a decision socket; an agent's
    PreToolUse hook asks it, and wash answers from an ordered rule table
    edited in Settings -> Agents. Off by default, and every failure resolves
    to the agent's own prompt — never to an allow.
  * agentd: new com.wash.agentd roster service. One sidebar row per agent
    across every terminal window — state, repo, branch, elapsed — sorted
    needs-input first, click to focus. Rows age out so a crashed terminal
    leaves no ghost.
  * agentd: answer permission requests from the sidebar (Allow / Always
    <rule> / Deny). "Always" writes the rule it names into the policy, so
    the table is taught rather than configured.
  * agentd: session history. Recent sessions survive a closed window or a
    reboot; Resume or Fork reopens one in a terminal in the right directory.
  * term: smart paste. Text copied out of a chat is repaired on the way in —
    invisible junk (non-breaking spaces, curly quotes, copied "$ " prompts,
    code fences) silently, and a soft-wrapped command offered as a preview
    before it changes structure. Includes a warning when a multi-line paste
    is about to hit a shell with bracketed paste off.
  * router: the per-channel scrollback ring grows to 4 MiB while nobody is
    attached and shrinks back afterwards, so work done with the lid shut is
    still there when you return. The terminal keeps 20,000 lines to match.
  * term: content no longer paints over the terminal scrollbar; the bar is
    themed with the rest of the chrome.
  * cli: new wash-agent-hook helper and `wash agent-hooks install|remove|
    status` for wiring the agent hooks into ~/.claude/settings.json.

